    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d779">

                <pb facs="0868" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg782"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-09-24"><hi rendition="#italic">September 24,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Adee states that the removal of the governor of Beirut was all the United
                    States Government asked, and commends Mr. Leishman’s disinclination to oppose
                    his appointment to Broussa.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
